/-!
# Two movers beyond the least frozen reading, the 12 clean frozen sets: the arrangement statement (GENERATED by `s2_gen_lean_clean_v1.py`)

Written 2026-10-23.  New file.  For each of the 12 frozen sets `F` (123, 124, 134, 234, 1234, 2345, 23456, 23457, 23467, 23567, 24567, 34567) with least
reading `a`, an arrangement of two movers whose disparities are BOTH strictly greater than `a` (no upper threshold) lands at the first lonely
instant, with the cascade sequence.  Same conclusion as `TwoMoverLandingAll2` (which needs both disparities at least `D0 = ⌈1/L⌉`).  Grades: [L];
[PROVISIONAL: covering] (the existence of a common clear instant in the first wide piece, a finite box cover per set) and [PROVISIONAL: counting tool]
by inheritance.  Not proved: movers at or below `a`, and frozen sets other than these 12.
-/

